<p>What is the probability of getting a head and an even number?</p>\n<p>A.</p>\n<p>1</p>\n<p>4</p>\n<p>B.</p>\n<p>2</p>\n<p>C.</p>\n<p>3</p>\n<p>D.</p>\n<p>6</p>\n<p>25. The scores 2, 4, 6 and 8 occur with frequencies 1, 3, 4 and 2 respectively. What is the mean score?</p>\n<h4>A. 5.0</h4>\n<h4>B. 5.4</h4>\n<h4>C. 6.0</h4>\n<h4>D. 5.6</h4>\n</section>\n\n<section class="uploaded-doc-page" data-page="9">\n<h2>Page 9</h2>\n<h3>Mathematics Diagnostic Baseline Assessment - Answer Key</h3>\n<p>Grade IX | Based on Grade VIII Mathematics | 25 Marks</p>\n<h3>Question Answer Diagnostic Concept</h3>\n<p>1 D Rational and irrational</p>\n<p>numbers</p>\n<p>2 B Recurring decimals</p>\n<p>3 C Square roots of decimals</p>\n<p>4 A Inverse proportion</p>\n<p>5 C Financial arithmetic / profit</p>\n<p>percentage</p>\n<p>6 D Power set</p>\n<p>7 D Properties of rational and</p>\n<p>irrational numbers</p>\n<p>8 A Linear inequality</p>\n<p>9 C Simplification of algebraic</p>\n<p>expressions</p>\n<p>10 B Algebraic identity</p>\n<h4>11 D Factorization</h4>\n<p>12 A Simultaneous linear</p>\n<p>equations</p>\n<p>13 C Laws of indices</p>\n<p>14 A Degree of a polynomial</p>\n<p>15 C Arithmetic sequence / nth</p>\n<p>term</p>\n<p>16 D Gradient of a straight line</p>\n<p>17 C Pythagoras theorem</p>\n<p>18 A Volume of a cone</p>\n<p>19 B Parallel lines and</p>\n<p>transversal</p>\n<p>20 D Arc length</p>\n<p>21 A Trigonometric ratio (sine)</p>\n<p>22 B Interior angles of polygons</p>\n<h4>23 B Median</h4>\n<p>24 A Combined probability</p>\n<p>25 B Mean from a frequency</p>\n<p>distribution</p>\n<p>[Table data, extracted with row/column structure]</p>\n</section>', 'file_name': 'ilovepdf_merged.pdf', 'rag_thread_id': 'user_12_conv_28_1790658144_9c0af362', 'conversation_id': 28, 'created_at': '2026-09-28T22:02:28.792632', 'updated_at': '2026-09-28T22:02:28.792650', 'is_public': True, 'has_child_version': False, 'parent_lesson_id': None, 'version': 1, 'lesson_id': 'L1790632948790', 'version_number': 1, 'parent_version_id': None, 'original_content': '# E2E Lesson AsIs 150007\n\n**Source document:** ilovepdf_merged.pdf\n\n<section class="uploaded-doc-page" data-page="2">\n<h2>Page 2</h2>\n<p>Mathematics Diagnostic Baseline Assessment for Grade IX students</p>\n<p>Based on Grade VIII Mathematics</p>\n<p>Time: 30 minutes | Total Marks: 25</p>\n<h4>Instructions</h4>\n<p>Choose the one best answer for each question. Attempt all questions. Each question carries 1 mark. You</p>\n<p>may use rough paper for working.</p>\n<p>Domain A. Number &amp; Operations and Sets</p>\n<p>1. Which pair contains one rational number and one irrational number?</p>\n<p>A. √25and 0.4</p>\n<p>B. √8and 𝜋</p>\n<p>C. 0.121212 …and</p>\n<p>7</p>\n<p>8</p>\n<p>D. √49and √10</p>\n<p>2. The number</p>\n<p>𝟓. 𝟏𝟖𝟏𝟖𝟏𝟖𝟏𝟖 …</p>\n<h4>is best described as</h4>\n<p>A. a rational terminating decimal</p>\n<p>B. a rational non-terminating recurring decimal</p>\n<p>C. an irrational number</p>\n<p>D. an integer</p>\n<p>3. What is</p>\n<p>√𝟎. 𝟎𝟎𝟖𝟏 ?</p>\n<h4>A. 0.9</h4>\n<h4>B. 0.009</h4>\n<h4>C. 0.09</h4>\n<h4>D. 0.081</h4>\n</section>\n\n<section class="uploaded-doc-page" data-page="3">\n<h2>Page 3</h2>\n<p>4. Eight workers can complete a job in 15 days. At the same rate, how many days would 12 workers take?</p>\n<p>A. 10 days</p>\n<p>B. 12 days</p>\n<p>C. 18 days</p>\n<p>D. 22.5 days</p>\n<p>5. A shopkeeper marks an item at Rs 4,000 and gives a 10% discount. The item originally cost the</p>\n<p>shopkeeper Rs 3,000.</p>\n<p>What percentage profit does the shopkeeper make on the cost price?</p>\n<h4>A. 15%</h4>\n<h4>B. 16</h4>\n<p>2</p>\n<p>3 %</p>\n<h4>C. 20%</h4>\n<h4>D. 33</h4>\n<p>1</p>\n<p>6. A set 𝑩 has 4 elements. How many elements are in its power set 𝑷(𝑩)?</p>\n<h4>A. 8</h4>\n<h4>B. 4</h4>\n<h4>C. 32</h4>\n<h4>D. 16</h4>\n<p>7. Which statement is always true?</p>\n<p>A. The product of two irrational numbers is always irrational.</p>\n<p>B. The square root of every positive integer is irrational.</p>\n<p>C. Every non-terminating decimal is irrational.</p>\n<p>D. The sum of a rational number and an irrational number is always irrational.</p>\n<h4>Domain B. Algebra</h4>\n</section>\n\n<section class="uploaded-doc-page" data-page="4">\n<h2>Page 4</h2>\n<h3>8. Solve</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>3𝑥 + 4 &gt; 10</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A. 𝑥 &lt; -2</p>\n<p>B. 𝑥 &gt; -2</p>\n<p>C. 𝑥 &lt; 2</p>\n<p>D. 𝑥 &gt; 2</p>\n<h4>9. Simplify</h4>\n<p>3𝑥(2𝑥 - 5) - 2𝑥(𝑥 - 4)</p>\n<p>A. 4𝑥2 - 23𝑥</p>\n<p>B. 8𝑥2 - 7𝑥</p>\n<p>C. 4𝑥2 - 7𝑥</p>\n<p>D. 4𝑥2 + 7𝑥</p>\n<p>10. Which expression is equal to</p>\n<p>(𝟑𝒙 - 𝟐)𝟐?</p>\n<p>A. 9𝑥2 - 4</p>\n<p>B. 9𝑥2 - 12𝑥 + 4</p>\n<p>C. 9𝑥2 - 6𝑥 + 4</p>\n<p>D. 6𝑥2 - 12𝑥 + 4</p>\n<p>11. Which is the correct factorization of</p>\n<p>𝒙𝟐 + 𝒙 - 𝟏𝟐?</p>\n<p>A. (𝑥 - 4)(𝑥 + 3)</p>\n<p>B. (𝑥 + 6)(𝑥 - 2)</p>\n<p>C. (𝑥 + 12)(𝑥 - 1)</p>\n<p>D. (𝑥 + 4)(𝑥 - 3)</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class="uploaded-doc-page" data-page="5">\n<h2>Page 5</h2>\n<p>12. Which ordered pair satisfies both equations?</p>\n<p>𝑥 + 𝑦 = 9</p>\n<p>𝑥 - 𝑦 = 3</p>\n<h4>A. (6, 3)</h4>\n<h4>B. (3, 6)</h4>\n<h4>C. (7, 2)</h4>\n<h4>D. (5, 4)</h4>\n<h4>13. Simplify</h4>\n<p>(𝑎3𝑏2)(𝑎2𝑏4)</p>\n<p>𝑎𝑏3</p>\n<p>A. 𝑎4𝑏6</p>\n<p>B. 𝑎5𝑏3</p>\n<p>C. 𝑎4𝑏3</p>\n<p>D. 𝑎6𝑏9</p>\n<p>14. What is the degree of the polynomial 𝟒𝒙𝟑𝒚𝟐 - 𝟕𝒙𝒚𝟒 + 𝟑?</p>\n<h4>A. 5</h4>\n<h4>B. 2</h4>\n<h4>C. 4</h4>\n<h4>D. 8</h4>\n<p>15. The arithmetic sequence 7, 12, 17, 22, ... continues in the same way. Which expression gives its nth</p>\n<p>term?</p>\n<p>A. 5n + 7</p>\n<p>B. 7n - 2</p>\n<p>C. 5n + 2</p>\n<p>D. 5n - 2</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class="uploaded-doc-page" data-page="6">\n<h2>Page 6</h2>\n<p>16. A straight line passes through the points (-1, 2) and (3, 10). What is the gradient of the line?</p>\n<h3>A. 1/2</h3>\n<h3>B. 4</h3>\n<h4>C. -2</h4>\n<h4>D. 2</h4>\n<h4>Domain C. Measurement &amp; Geometry</h4>\n<p>17. A ladder 15 m long is placed against a wall. If its upper end reaches the height of 12 m along the wall,</p>\n<p>then find the distance of the foot of the ladder from the wall.</p>\n<p>A. 3 m</p>\n<p>B. 6 m</p>\n<p>C. 9 m</p>\n<p>D. 12 m</p>\n<p>18. A cone has a base area of 𝟑𝟎 cm𝟐and a perpendicular height of 9 cm.</p>\n<p>What is its volume?</p>\n<p>A. 90 cm3</p>\n<p>B. 270 cm3</p>\n<p>C. 30 cm3</p>\n<p>D. 810 cm3</p>\n<p>19. Choose the correct statement.</p>\n<p>A. If two parallel lines are intersected by a transversal, the interior angles on the same side of the</p>\n<p>transversal are congruent.</p>\n<p>B. If two parallel lines are intersected by a transversal, the interior angles on the same side of the</p>\n<p>transversal are supplementary.</p>\n<p>C. The diagonals of every rectangle bisect each other at right angles.</p>\n<p>D. If a transversal intersects any two lines, the alternate interior angles are always congruent.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class="uploaded-doc-page" data-page="7">\n<h2>Page 7</h2>\n<p>20. A circle has radius 7 cm. An arc subtends an angle of 𝟗𝟎∘at the centre.</p>\n<p>Using 𝜋 =</p>\n<p>22</p>\n<p>7 , what is the length of the arc?</p>\n<p>A. 5.5 cm</p>\n<p>B. 22 cm</p>\n<p>C. 44 cm</p>\n<p>D. 11 cm</p>\n<p>21. In a right-angled triangle, if the opposite side = 4 cm and the hypotenuse = 5 cm, then 𝑠𝑖𝑛 𝜃 =?</p>\n<p>A.</p>\n<p>4</p>\n<p>5</p>\n<p>B.</p>\n<p>3</p>\n<p>C.</p>\n<p>D.</p>\n<p>1</p>\n<p>2</p>\n<p>22. What is the sum of the interior angles of a 7-sided polygon?</p>\n<h4>A. 720∘</h4>\n<h4>B. 900∘</h4>\n<h4>C. 1080∘</h4>\n<h4>D. 1260∘</h4>\n<h4>D. Statistics &amp; Probability</h4>\n<h4>23. Find the median of</h4>\n<p>12, 4, 7, 2, 5</p>\n<h4>A. 6</h4>\n<h4>B. 5</h4>\n<h4>C. 7</h4>\n<h4>D. 10</h4>\n</section>\n\n<section class="uploaded-doc-page" data-page="8">\n<h2>Page 8</h2>\n<p>24. A fair coin is tossed and a fair six-sided die is rolled.</p>\n<p>What is the probability of getting a head and an even number?</p>\n<p>A.</p>\n<p>1</p>\n<p>4</p>\n<p>B.</p>\n<p>2</p>\n<p>C.</p>\n<p>3</p>\n<p>D.</p>\n<p>6</p>\n<p>25. The scores 2, 4, 6 and 8 occur with frequencies 1, 3, 4 and 2 respectively. What is the mean score?</p>\n<h4>A. 5.0</h4>\n<h4>B. 5.4</h4>\n<h4>C. 6.0</h4>\n<h4>D. 5.6</h4>\n</section>\n\n<section class="uploaded-doc-page" data-page="9">\n<h2>Page 9</h2>\n<h3>Mathematics Diagnostic Baseline Assessment - Answer Key</h3>\n<p>Grade IX | Based on Grade VIII Mathematics | 25 Marks</p>\n<h3>Question Answer Diagnostic Concept</h3>\n<p>1 D Rational and irrational</p>\n<p>numbers</p>\n<p>2 B Recurring decimals</p>\n<p>3 C Square roots of decimals</p>\n<p>4 A Inverse proportion</p>\n<p>5 C Financial arithmetic / profit</p>\n<p>percentage</p>\n<p>6 D Power set</p>\n<p>7 D Properties of rational and</p>\n<p>irrational numbers</p>\n<p>8 A Linear inequality</p>\n<p>9 C Simplification of algebraic</p>\n<p>expressions</p>\n<p>10 B Algebraic identity</p>\n<h4>11 D Factorization</h4>\n<p>12 A Simultaneous linear</p>\n<p>equations</p>\n<p>13 C Laws of indices</p>\n<p>14 A Degree of a polynomial</p>\n<p>15 C Arithmetic sequence / nth</p>\n<p>term</p>\n<p>16 D Gradient of a straight line</p>\n<p>17 C Pythagoras theorem</p>\n<p>18 A Volume of a cone</p>\n<p>19 B Parallel lines and</p>\n<p>transversal</p>\n<p>20 D Arc length</p>\n<p>21 A Trigonometric ratio (sine)</p>\n<p>22 B Interior angles of polygons</p>\n<h4>23 B Median</h4>\n<p>24 A Combined probability</p>\n<p>25 B Mean from a frequency</p>\n<p>distribution</p>\n<p>[Table data, extracted with row/column structure]</p>\n</section>', 'draft_content': None, 'status': 'finalized', 'teacher_name': 'e2e_teacher', 'is_original': True}]
